<title>SWEDEN: SKF posts 29 pct drop in 1996 profits.</title>
<headline>SKF posts 29 pct drop in 1996 profits.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bearings manufacturer SKF AB reported on Thursday results for the 12 months ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  2,412 vs  3,389</p>
<p> Sales					33,589 vs 36,700</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (SKR) per share    5.25 vs   5.25</p>
<p> Production costs			 23,482 vs 25,079</p>
<p> Sales and Admin costs		   6,209 vs  6,367</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,392 vs  1,360</p>
<p> Operating profit			  2,874 vs  4,000</p>
<p> Net financial items	     CHARGE  462 vs     611 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					   701 vs  1,301</p>
<p> Minorities				     19 vs     30</p>
<p>Earnings per share after tax (SKR)  14.95 vs  18.20  Net income				  1,692 vs  2,058</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll found that the market expected SKF to report a profit after financial items of 2.13 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
